# LLM — Stage 3 (context) and Stage 4 (analyst).
# Deployment decision: BOTH stages run foundation-sec-reasoning. qwen3.5:4b is
# deliberately NOT pulled. See CLAUDE.md "Deployment-specific decisions" for the
# latency trade-off this accepts.
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://172.20.24.225:11434/v1
#LLM_MODEL=foundation-sec-reasoning:latesthttps://new-event-coral-tube.trycloudflare.com
#LLM_API_KEY=sk-no-auth

LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
LLM_API_KEY=AQ.Ab8RN6Ic4ea8kf42LXrvHpTwPdJGdYNvNto7kj7OJHVseaLvOA
LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# Gemini test session, 2026-08-23 — raised per user request ("free trial,
# no limitation now"). Real live-confirmed limits for this model (GET
# /v1beta/models/gemini-3.6-flash): inputTokenLimit=1048576,
# outputTokenLimit=65536, "thinking": true (spends a variable, invisible
# slice of max_tokens on internal reasoning before visible output — see
# config.py's STAGE_3/4_DESIRED_MAX_TOKENS comment for the live repro).
# LLM_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS set to the real inputTokenLimit so the
# prompt-vs-budget cap in nodes/context.py|analyze.py's _capped_max_tokens
# stops constraining anything for this pipeline's actual prompt sizes
# (a few thousand tokens, nowhere near 1M) — effectively a no-op ceiling.
# STAGE_3/4_DESIRED_MAX_TOKENS raised well past the old 4000/2000 to leave
# headroom for Gemini's hidden thinking tokens on top of the real JSON
# output. These are Gemini-specific overrides — remove/lower them when
# reverting LLM_BASE_URL back to the original foundation-sec-reasoning
# deployment, whose 8192-token real context window these would exceed.
# Raised again, live-caught 2026-08-23: a real Stage 4 call against the
# "judge every observable" design (21 real case_observables on this alert
# alone) hit finish_reason="length" at STAGE_4_DESIRED_MAX_TOKENS=4000 --
# completion_tokens=1004 but total_tokens=9202 against a 5221-token prompt,
# meaning ~2977 tokens went to invisible thinking before any visible JSON,
# leaving no room for the now much longer actionable_observables array.
# 16000 gives real headroom above both observed costs combined.
LLM_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS=1048576
STAGE_3_DESIRED_MAX_TOKENS=8000
STAGE_4_DESIRED_MAX_TOKENS=16000

# Generous on purpose: this Ollama host runs the model on CPU during
# development/testing (production is expected to run on GPU, much faster).
# A live-verified schema-constrained Stage 3 call took ~69s on a small toy
# alert; a real EnrichedEvidence prompt will take longer. This is a config
# value only — nodes/context.py's call logic does not branch on CPU vs GPU.
# Tighten this once running against a GPU-backed endpoint.
STAGE_3_LLM_TIMEOUT=600

# Same reasoning as STAGE_3_LLM_TIMEOUT above, same host/model — Stage 4's
# sanitized-summary prompt is smaller than Stage 3's full EnrichedEvidence,
# but this deployment's Stage 3 real calls still took 271.1s and 323.2s on
# CPU (see tests/test_context.py, REPO-STATUS.md), well past the 180s
# config.py default. Config value only — nodes/analyze.py does not branch
# on CPU vs GPU. Tighten once running against a GPU-backed endpoint.
STAGE_4_LLM_TIMEOUT=600


